  "title": "The glue block one size past, on the 10-line trisum glue",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "One size past ticket A, on the 10-line trisum glue (TRISUM-READ's seeds 6 and 36, which give isomorphic glues; cycle rank 11), the signed glue's creation map takes 1,526 values on the 2,048 switching classes and 429 on their 576 orbits under the glue's 4 automorphisms; 92 of the 98 groups of classes sharing a block span several orbits and 76 mix solution counts. The largest group is exactly the 190 classes at which no far side creates at any entry, from 66 orbits, with 60 to 110 solutions. A pair of classes from two orbits with different solution counts has identical glue blocks on its plain edge-atom spaces, and adding census 6 under every order of the gluing line separates neither that pair nor ticket A's pair. The Pfaffian class is again the only class without solutions, and no other class has its block.",
